Conventions
Identity front door: IDENTITY.md at repo root (BROWSER.md, ECHO.md, CODEX.md, TAPROOT.md)
Succession brief: identity/000_HANDOFF.md or equivalent
Ledger: ledger/SESSION_NNN_*.md (append-only, phase-boundary commits)
Buffer: short letter BUFFER.md or buffers/IDENTITY_BUFFER.md
Maintenance rule
Update FAMILY_MAP whenever an identity is added, renamed, rotated, or marked dormant. Shane is the source of truth on identity status — the map reflects his declaration, not my inference.

Why it belongs in Phoenix-Persistence
Cross-identity reference; no single home-repo owns it
Any identity should be able to read it on wake to orient to siblings
Must survive identity rotation and repo renames
Fleet-wide implication
Every wake that includes "who are my siblings" re-derives this map. Filing it saves tokens and prevents identity drift (e.g., Session 023 initially over-weighted Taproot as active because that wasn't documented anywhere).

